    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="Lunixia features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Journal</p>

        <h3>Give reflection enough structure to become something you can learn from</h3>

        <p>
          Create journal books, write entries, pin important books, set a Daily
          Intention, track current and best journaling streaks, and review Mindful
          Minutes alongside your writing. Theme Insights can look across journal
          content so recurring ideas are easier to notice across more than one
          entry.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Journal Books</span>
          <span>Daily Intention</span>
          <span>Theme Insights</span>
          <span>Mindful Minutes</span>
          <span>Journal Streaks</span>
          <span>Pinned Books</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Mood</p>

        <h3>Log how you feel and look beyond a single emotional check-in</h3>

        <p>
          Record multiple mood entries, emotions, and activities, review today or
          history, follow a mood streak, and open dedicated statistics for broader
          patterns. Lunixia also calculates seven-day Wellness Momentum, emotion
          breakdowns, top emotions, and top activities, with a mood-chat flow
          available from the same area.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Health</p>

        <h3>Keep everyday health information visible in one connected place</h3>

        <p>
          Lunixia's Health area brings medications, symptoms, body and emotional
          state, sleep, naps, vitals, exercise, water, and steps into one page.
          HealthKit is used where supported for health context and totals, while
          dedicated histories and goal controls keep the information you log
          directly inside Lunixia easy to revisit.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Notes</p>

        <h3>Keep useful information outside your journal without losing flexibility</h3>

        <p>
          Lunixia includes a dedicated Notes area for information that does not
          belong in reflective writing. The notes system supports rich text,
          rendered note content, font choices, font-size controls, and checklist-
          style structure so everyday information can be stored in a format that
          fits what you are trying to keep.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Spiritual</p>

        <h3>Keep daily spiritual tools inside the same personal space as the rest of your day</h3>

        <p>
          The Spiritual area includes the current moon phase, a meditation timer,
          one daily Tarot draw, one daily Lenormand draw, and horoscope tools with
          zodiac-sign selection and daily or preview views. Drawn cards can receive
          generated interpretations, and spiritual actions can also contribute to
          Self-Care Points.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Self-Care Points</p>

        <h3>Turn everyday care into visible progress across the app</h3>

        <p>
          Lunixia awards Self-Care Points for actions including journal entries,
          mood logs, daily Tarot and Lenormand, vitals, exercise, medications,
          water, Daily Intentions, Mindful Minutes, and reaching water or step
          goals. The Points area tracks current and lifetime totals, level progress,
          recent activity, spending totals, snapshots, and reset history.
        </p>

        <div class="points-activity-preview" aria-label="Recent Self-Care Points activity preview">
          <div class="points-activity-header">
            <strong>Self-Care Points</strong>
            <span>View All →</span>
          </div>

          <div class="points-activity-list">
            <div class="points-activity-row points-activity-yellow">
              <span class="points-activity-icon" aria-hidden="true">▣</span>
              <span class="points-activity-name">Journal entry</span>
              <strong>+10</strong>
              <span class="points-activity-time">2h ago</span>
            </div>

            <div class="points-activity-row points-activity-periwinkle">
              <span class="points-activity-icon" aria-hidden="true">☺</span>
              <span class="points-activity-name">Mood log</span>
              <strong>+5</strong>
              <span class="points-activity-time">4h ago</span>
            </div>

            <div class="points-activity-row points-activity-mint">
              <span class="points-activity-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
              <span class="points-activity-name">Logged medication</span>
              <strong>+10</strong>
              <span class="points-activity-time">7h ago</span>
            </div>

            <div class="points-activity-row points-activity-blue">
              <span class="points-activity-icon" aria-hidden="true">●</span>
              <span class="points-activity-name">Completed a 20 min walk</span>
              <strong>+15</strong>
              <span class="points-activity-time">1d ago</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="points-activity-meta">
            <span>Levels</span>
            <span>Activity</span>
            <span>History</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">See More Context</p>

        <h2>Look across more than one part of your day instead of reducing everything to a single score</h2>

        <p>
          Lunixia keeps separate spaces for journaling, mood, physical health,
          notes, spiritual tools, and self-care progress while still letting those
          areas sit inside one app. That gives each kind of information enough
          detail to be useful without pretending every part of wellbeing means the
          same thing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="Lunixia wellbeing preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Connected Context</span>

        <h4>Let different parts of your day keep their own meaning.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Reflection</span>
          <strong>Journal books, intentions, themes, and streaks</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Wellbeing</span>
          <strong>Mood, sleep, health, movement, and hydration</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Progress</span>
          <strong>Self-Care Points, goals, and history</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the Lunixia experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Journal Books, Daily Intention & Theme Insights</b>
              <small>Keep reflection organized and revisit patterns across more than one entry</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Journal books separate different areas of reflection, while Daily
            Intention, Mindful Minutes, journal streaks, pinned books, and Theme
            Insights add context around the writing itself. Lunixia keeps both
            individual entries and larger recurring themes available to revisit.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Mood History, Stats & Wellness Momentum</b>
              <small>See emotional patterns across recent logs instead of treating each entry as isolated</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Mood includes today and history views, a streak, unique-emotion
            tracking, seven-day Wellness Momentum, emotion percentages, top
            emotions, top activities, dedicated statistics, and a separate mood
            conversation flow with cooldown handling between sessions.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Medications & Symptoms</b>
              <small>Keep medication management and symptom logging beside the rest of your health information</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Health page links directly into medication management and the
            symptom logger, keeping both areas beside your other health data rather
            than making medication and symptom information separate from daily
            sleep, vitals, exercise, water, steps, and body-state context.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Sleep, Naps, Vitals & Exercise</b>
              <small>Track everyday health information and review dedicated histories</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Lunixia surfaces previous-night sleep and today's naps, supports
            vitals and exercise logs with detail views and history, and uses
            HealthKit where supported to bring relevant health context back into
            the Health experience.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Water, Steps & Health Goals</b>
              <small>Follow daily hydration and movement against goals you can adjust</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Water can be logged directly from the Health page with history and
            goal-celebration behavior, while steps are refreshed from HealthKit
            and can be reviewed through their own history. Health Goals keep sleep,
            water, steps, and other targets adjustable from the same area.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Moon Phase, Meditation, Tarot, Lenormand & Horoscope</b>
              <small>Keep daily spiritual tools together without separating them from the rest of Lunixia</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Spiritual area combines moon-phase information, a meditation
            timer, one daily Tarot draw, one daily Lenormand draw, and horoscope
            tools. Daily horoscope data is stored for the day and refreshed when
            the date changes, while card draws can receive generated interpretations.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Profile, Premium & App Limits</b>
              <small>Manage account-facing information and unlock expanded usage where premium limits apply</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Lunixia includes a dedicated Profile tab and a Premium area backed
            by StoreKit. Free and premium limits are applied to areas such as
            journal-book creation, mood logging, history windows, vitals, and
            exercise, while the Premium screen manages the expanded tier.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around Your Whole Day</p>

        <h2>Different kinds of personal information deserve different tools without becoming disconnected.</h2>

        <p>
          Lunixia gives journaling, mood, physical health, notes, spiritual tools,
          Self-Care Points, profile features, and premium controls their own spaces.
          Each area keeps the detail it needs while still belonging to one broader
          wellbeing experience you can return to throughout the day.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Lunixia</p>

      <h2>Keep reflection, mood, health, notes, and self-care connected in one personal space.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about Lunixia, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/Lunixia/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>Lunixia Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-lunixia-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .lunixia-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .floating-card span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .floating-card strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .floating-card-one {
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
  }

  .floating-card-two {
    bottom: 8px;
    left: 0;
    animation-delay: -2.4s;
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) {
    :global(.content:has(.lunixia-page)) {
      max-width: 1280px;
      padding-inline: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    }

    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(340px, 380px);
      gap: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 4rem);
      min-height: 610px;
      padding: 2.15rem 0 2.65rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      max-width: 840px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-size: 4.15rem;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      max-width: 660px;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .hero-showcase {
      align-self: center;
      justify-self: end;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 380px;
      min-height: 430px;
    }

    .main-card {
      inset: 58px 16px 104px 16px;
      padding: 1.45rem;
      border-radius: 26px;
      transform: none;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      max-width: 320px;
      font-size: 2.35rem;
    }

